course: dictionary
lesson: 1695
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Chuff can be the puffing sound of a steam train, or a way of saying you feel very pleased. «Callum scored a hat-trick, and Dad was so chuffed.» Dad is not making a train noise. He is pleased, so chuffed means very pleased.
explain: A word can also change its shape to fit the sentence. Chuff is a verb (chuff, chuffs, chuffed, chuffing), a noun (a chuff) and an adjective (chuffed). In «Tadhg is chuffed for a week», chuffed is an adjective describing how Tadhg feels.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Wynne is half insulted and half chuffed that Gwil cares.» Try "half pleased" instead. It fits, so chuffed means pleased here, even though Wynne's feelings are mixed.
explain: Chuffed is mostly used in British everyday speech, and it is informal, so it is fine for chatting with friends. For school writing, you could say "very pleased" instead.
fact: Chuff can mean the puffing sound of a steam train, as in «chuff-chuff».
fact: «Chuffed» (UK, informal) means very pleased.
fact: «Chuffed to bits» means very, very pleased.
fact: «Tigers greet each other with a friendly puffing sound called chuffing.»
fact: «Chuffing» is a mild swear word in some places, so leave it out of school.
exercise: «The old steam engine began to chuff out of the station.» What does chuff mean here? | A kind of cake | A bright shiny colour | *The puffing sound of a steam train | A loud shout of anger
exercise: «Dad was so chuffed when Callum scored a hat-trick.» What does chuffed mean? | Cross and rude | Lost and confused | *Very pleased | Very tired after a long day
exercise: «Tadhg is chuffed (very pleased) for a week.» Find and copy the adjective in this sentence. | *chuffed | Tadhg | week | for
test: «Tadhg is chuffed to bits, so he grins all day.» What does chuffed to bits mean? | Stuck in the mud | Hungry and cold | *Very, very pleased | Sleepy after a long night
test: «Wynne is half insulted and half chuffed that Gwil cares.» Which swap fits best for chuffed? | Half a mile | Half asleep | *Half pleased | Half-hearted
exam: Ella reads «Tigers greet each other with a friendly puffing sound called chuffing.» What is a chuff here? | A wild river | *A soft puffing sound used as a greeting | A type of stripe | Something a tiger eats
